# Reviewing changes in `scripts/hooks/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`scripts/hooks/REVIEW.md`** for
any changed path under `scripts/hooks/`. That map cites rule IDs from
`scripts/hooks/AGENTS.md` (HOOK-1/2/3 — the Track A invariants) — it never restates the
rule text.

Rules enforced here (LLM-judged; the hooks themselves are the deterministic rung):
- HOOK-1 — `PostToolUse`/`afterFileEdit` never blocks the edit (formatter is advisory;
  `failClosed: false` is an intentional, scoped deviation).
- HOOK-2 — `PreToolUse`/`beforeShellExecution` is safety-only and thin (deny-list guard).
- HOOK-3 — fail safe on malformed input (Cursor hooks fail OPEN by default; safety hooks
  set `failClosed: true`).

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
